By Jamelle Bouie
Opinion Columnist

All right, so obviously, this isn’t a vegetarian recipe. It’s easy enough to make vegetarian — just omit the bacon. But if you are a meat eater, let me make the case for treating these beans as if they were meat. With the right ingredients and the right technique, I think you can produce a pot of beans that rivals a beef stew. Admittedly, you’ll want to use a good beef stock (I happened to have some beef stock in the free…";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1700535124;}s:7:"creator";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1700535124;s:2:"ip";s:12:"71.210.32.57";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:36:"recipes:smoky_pinto_beans_with_bacon";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:7:"created";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:2213;}}}